<title>PORTUGAL: Escudo dips on mark, ignores stronger dollar.</title>
<headline>Escudo dips on mark, ignores stronger dollar.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo slipped against the mark, following the lead of the Spanish peseta which eased on news that the Bank of Spain had cut its repo rate 25 basis points.</p>
<p>The Portuguese currency was trading at 99.98/100.01 to the mark against its 99.87/90 close on Monday. It was already at the low end of the day's predicted trading range of 99.85/100.00, dealers said.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
